@TGT
Feature: a target whose fitness checks are converted scenarios

  Planted for @SCN-STG-005's @integration arm and used TWICE — this tree is byte-identical in
  the scn-tags-converted-no-manifest fixture beside it, and only the package.json differs.

  Both scenarios below carry the fitness axis tag and their @SCN and nothing else, which is
  the whole of what a converted check's scenario says about itself: the tag names the axis and
  the COMMAND is on the configured row. Neither names a tier, and neither carries a bare
  check tag any configured row names — so both red the shipped command as tags that mean nothing
  here unless the axis word is grammar in its own right.

  THE PAIR IS THE RULING RATHER THAN AN ACCIDENT OF THE PLANT. Only one of these two @SCNs is
  named by a manifest entry, and after 3F-3582 that difference declares nothing: both scenarios
  raise their fitness Evidence Obligation from the tag. Both are admitted by the tag grammar,
  which is what this fixture is for. Whether anything ANSWERS either obligation belongs
  to @SCN-LNT-020, which reds an unanswered one on its own row by id. Redding it here too would
  put half of one fault in a second place with the wrong remedy attached — "this word means nothing
  here", said to an author whose scenario names the one axis the model has.

  AND THE SISTER TREE CONFIGURES NO ROWS AT ALL, where both scenarios still pass. Which words
  name a CHECK is the target's answer; which axis a scenario is ON is the model's, exactly as
  `unit` is — so the axis word is not the target's to grant or to withhold, and a grammar
  gating it on the manifest would red here while the obligation rule — which reads the word with
  no such gate — was naming SCN-TGT-001 and SCN-TGT-002 as scenarios on that very axis.

  @fitness @SCN-TGT-001
  Scenario: the codebase stays inside the complexity thresholds

  @fitness @SCN-TGT-002
  Scenario: a converted scenario no configured row names
